hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2878","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani, narrated to us al-Mu'tamir who said: I heard Ayman ibn Nabil say: I heard Qudamah ibn 'Abdullah — and he is the son of 'Ammar — say: \I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr) upon his camel named Sahba'"","" neither striking (the camel) nor driving (it harshly) nor saying 'To me!' (i.e."","" urging it on in a harsh manner).\""\n\n\n\nCHAPTER:"""""
